4.197.m:
Durvāsas said:
"Listen attentively, O fair-browed lady, to the story of your past self;
O fortunate one, I know your past history in its entirety.

4.207.m:
The venerable Kṛṣṇa said:
Votive observances, gifts, and duties have been revealed to you, O king;
since this is the foundation of dharma, therefore be devoted to dharma.

